  "summary": "SparkGLM on two directly connected DGX Sparks (TP-2 pair) or four cabled as a daisy chain (TP-4), serving nvidia/GLM-5.3-Flash-FP4-Local as published with DFlash2 speculative decoding: four requests of up to 1M tokens. Options: --sparks 2|4 and --drafter v81|v80|dflash2. Additive only: no default model, no aliases.",
  "description": "This recipe installs SparkGLM 0.3.1 at the immutable product revision recorded in backends/atlas-sparkglm/pins-0.3.1.json, on two Sparks (--sparks 2, a TP-2 pair over the private fabric) or four (--sparks 4, TP-4 over a switchless daisy chain, rank 0-1-2-3 along the cables), with any of three drafters (--drafter v81 or v80, Enntity's from a private repository, or --drafter dflash2, incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2). Without --drafter, two Sparks use v81 and four use dflash2. Setup remembers the options it installed with. LLooM owns orchestration, admission, worker-first startup, readiness, routing and telemetry. The Atlas engine image is built from Enntity/sparkglm by that repository's install/build.sh; LLooM commits no engine source. The engine (Atlas-Inf/atlas, on the Enntity/atlas spark branch) is AGPL-3.0-only and runs from its own container image. Setup acquires the pinned checkpoint and the selected drafter and pulls the pinned image from GHCR by its immutable manifest digest (image.reference; the mutable tag is never pulled); the serving path only ever starts the prepared image. The checkpoint is served as published, with no overlay. One image serves both sizes. At TP-2 the release qualified on 2026-11-03 against 0.3.0 with the v80 drafter (identical greedy output and prompt logprobs, 109/109 live checks; sparkglm-research experiments/qual-20261103); 0.3.1 has not been run at TP-4 yet, and has not been qualified with v81 (in Enntity's drafter benchmark on a two-Spark Atlas server, 2026-11-05, v81 was 2-6% faster than v80 on code and structured output with identical output text).",
  "license": {
    "id": "MIT",
    "name": "Recipe metadata, launcher and orchestration"
  },
  "provenance": {
    "createdBy": "lloom",
    "generatedBy": "manual-curated",
    "source": "SparkGLM 0.3.1: Enntity/sparkglm 33fe02f83a9edf96ae38ebe4fc6a8ec8e7603f90 (tag v0.3.1, install tree e7af504a3dfde2652e05de9c32304ffd3de7f2fa), engine Enntity/atlas spark @ 5f79b46ba7b0e8b14f8b2966cca9e2546f18560d (Atlas-Inf main 2f9c37083; AGPL-3.0-only, recorded in the image's /opt/atlas/source-manifest.json). The install pulls ghcr.io/enntity/atlas-sparkglm@sha256:8e1e378b61f2633283fc86772b78f3524220255064630cc069d64b70cc5df7e0 by digest (pins-0.3.1.json; the tag ghcr.io/enntity/atlas-sparkglm:e7af504a3dfd is never pulled), and each host verifies the image's io.enntity.sparkglm.install-tree label, arm64 architecture, both profiles and the engine commit. Model nvidia/GLM-5.3-Flash-FP4-Local revision 76348ddb2be2e35e39ecfc00e75dc07703f4f3d5 (NVIDIA Open Model Agreement; base model MIT) is served as published. Drafters: Enntity/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2-enntity revision ee5ed56e3ed2e59fd2d5177fe6773b2f6fb4aa80 (v81, tag v81, model.safetensors sha256 d14e1edb080711d4; private), Enntity/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2-enntity-v80 revision 8416cdfbf4cfb302b86a058cb5f5b89f891350c0 (v80, the same repository under its earlier name; private) and incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2 revision 7d74cdd881ed7e32c31175984a67823127b66cfe (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0). Qualified at TP-2 with v80 on 2026-11-03 against 0.3.0 (sparkglm-research experiments/qual-20261103); not yet run at TP-4."
  },
